  "body": "Blink and WebKit do not align with the spec's simple \"computed\" model for determining value and defaultValue. Instead they seem to use *child* observers (*not* descendant observers) to sync the default value with the *descendant* text content.\r\n\r\nThis causes them to fail [the relevant test](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/forms/the-output-element/mutations.window.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=mutations), although that test is broken anyway further down in the assert chain. (The latter is being fixed in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/28161.)\r\n\r\nA stripped down demonstration is https://jsbin.com/degojafare/1/edit?html,output\r\n\r\nIMO this is best classified as a Blink/WebKit bug as it's super-weird that they do not take descendant modifications into account, only child mutations. Also, the spec behavior (which Gecko matches) is much nicer and simpler as it doesn't require any observers at all.\r\n\r\nAny thoughts @rniwa @josepharhar? I am pretty sure this is an extreme edge case so aligning Blink and WebKit to Gecko and the spec shouldn't cause compat problems.\r\n\r\nAlso, Gecko does not match the spec/Blink/WebKit's reset behavior, as seen from the [wpt.fyi dashboard](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/forms/the-output-element/mutations.window.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=mutations), so there's plenty of non-interop to go around here.",
